Hello Dr. Tucker-Drob,

Thank you so much for your kind advice. I've been mulling over multiple references, and now have a clear understanding of your point. I've generated a model below (please refer to lavaan syntax below and schematic picture).  I believe that this model represents my goal: I'm trying to get the residual variance associated for aneurysm development (the "atypical" latent variable)  after subtracting out total variances associated with HTN or smoking. The output of the model fitting is included below.

However, I'm having difficulty with a few questions:

(1) I'm not sure why Factor3_Atypical is correlating with variable aneurysm by 1.0. This makes me concerned that the model I've created is incorrect.

(2) I'm not sure why the CFI value is negative. and I'm having a tough time finding solutions online.

(3) Do you have any suggestions on how to improve the SRMR? Would it be to find other summary statistics for HTN and smoking that better correlate with aneurysm summary statistics with lower pvalues?

Thank you so very much for your help! I truly appreciate your patience and kind advice.

Joseph Shin

model<-'F1_HTN =~ HTN+ Smoking + ANEURYSM
F2_SMOKING =~ Smoking + ANEURYSM
F3_ATYPICAL=~ANEURYSM

F1_HTN ~~1*F1_HTN
F2_SMOKING ~~1*F2_SMOKING
F3_ATYPICAL ~~ 1*F3_ATYPICAL
F1_HTN~~0*F2_SMOKING
F1_HTN~~0*F3_ATYPICAL
F2_SMOKING~~0*F3_ATYPICAL

HTN~~0*HTN
HTN~~0*Smoking
HTN~~0*ANEURYSM
Smoking~~0*Smoking
Smoking~~0*ANEURYSM
ANEURYSM~~0*ANEURYSM'

